ul.li:
Security mechanisms binding bundles to specific EIDs (BPSec
                ) would break if routers modified
                destinations

section.t:
This specification requests IANA to assign a permanent block type
code from the "Bundle Block Types" registry (created by
). Until IANA assignment:

figure.sourcecode:
/ CBOR Extended Diagnostic Notation (EDN) /
{
    0: 0.75,                    / Default probability /
    1: [
        [300, 0.5],             / To relay node 300: 0.5 /
        [100, 1.0]              / To orbiter node 100: 1.0 /
    ],
    5: 1                        / metric-type: cgr-confidence /
}

ul.li:
concerns administrative record types;
             CPB is an extension block, not an administrative record, so
             RFC 9713 does not apply directly.

CBOR float16 encoding with deterministic encoding rules;
              format version field (key 7); per-path array size guidance
              as SHOULD with local enforcement on constrained links.
